    summaryEn: "Investing visuals: AMZN Q2 Rev $180.2B (est $178.5B) · EPS $2.55 (est $1.99, +28% beat) · Op Income $23.85B (est $22.60B) · AWS $30.0B (+20% YoY) · Q3 guide $200B+ (est $198.28B). Combines with yesterday's 3× net income and CAPEX $220B.",
    bodyEn: "■ Print Details\n\nToday from Investing visuals on AMZN Q2 2026:\n\n**Core Metrics**\n- **Revenue**: $180.2B (est $178.5B)\n- **Op Income**: $23.85B (est $22.60B)\n- **AWS Revenue**: $30.0B (+20% YoY)\n- **EPS**: $2.55 (est $1.99, +28% beat)\n\n**Q3 Guidance**\n- **Revenue**: $200B+ (est $198.28B)\n\n■ Combined With Yesterday's Report\n\nYesterday's (7/31) AMZN Q2 report:\n- Net income $62.6B (3× growth)\n- 2026 CAPEX $200B → $220B raised\n- 2027 to rise more\n- Stock +8%\n\nToday's report adds (a) revenue/EPS/AWS detailed metrics, (b) Q3 guidance confirmation. Two reports illuminate earnings from different angles.\n\n**Comprehensive Print Profile**\n- Revenue: $180.2B (record)\n- Op Income: $23.85B\n- Net income: $62.6B\n- EPS: $2.55 (+28% beat)\n- AWS: $30.0B (+20%)\n- CAPEX: $200B → $220B raised\n- Q3 guide: $200B+\n\nBull across all axes.\n\n■ Meaning of AWS $30B (+20% YoY)\n\nAWS Q2 revenue $30B:\n- +20% YoY\n- 21% of today's separate report on cloud infra Q2 $142B\n- Relatively mature growth vs Azure 43% and other GCP growth rates\n\nCounter-view:\n- 20% growth still solid but relatively lower than Azure 43%\n- AWS lead may be shrinking in hyperscaler market share competition\n- But absolute revenue scale still dominant\n\n■ Meaning of EPS $2.55 (+28% Beat)\n\n+28% beat is substantial surprise:\n1. **Cost management**: Successful cost management vs revenue\n2. **AWS margin**: AWS high margin drives EPS\n3. **Ad revenue**: Prime Video / Sponsored Ads expansion\n4. **Retail efficiency**: Cost cuts via AI automation etc.\n\n■ Meaning of Q3 Guidance $200B+\n\nQ3 revenue guide $200B+ = +11% QoQ growth from Q2 $180.2B expected. Reflects (1) peak season (back-to-school / shopping season prep), (2) AWS continued growth, (3) ad revenue expansion, (4) Prime Day effect reflection.\n\n■ Combined With Recent Hyperscaler Flow\n\n- **7/24**: GOOGL 2026 CAPEX $200B\n- **7/28**: OpenAI Ohio $500B DC\n- **7/29**: META×BLK 1 GW DC $14B\n- **7/30**: MSFT Q4 Azure $100B · Copilot 30M+\n- **7/31**: AMZN net income 3× · CAPEX $220B\n- **Today**: MSFT +$400B · AMZN detail · hyper CAPEX $155B · cloud $142B\n\nHyperscaler bull cycle comprehensively confirmed in earnings season.\n\n■ Counter-view\n\n(1) EPS +28% beat may trigger short-term reversal risk, (2) AWS 20% growth relatively lower than Azure 43% · market share stagnation concerns, (3) Today's unusualwhales mention of AMZN 25% drop prediction (screenshot 7.40.41) · counter-view exists, (4) Q3 $200B+ guide realization confirmation in next earnings.\n\n■ Watch Next\n\n(1) Q3 revenue realization · guide consistency, (2) AWS 20% growth continuity, (3) Kuiper direct-to-phone 3,232 satellite filing (7/29 report) progress, (4) Zoox 2,500-unit exemption utilization (vs today's Cybercab regulatory edge).\n\ninvestus.kr SRP Chief Investment Officer",
