    summaryEn: "Evan D: 4 companies (AMZN·META·GOOGL·MSFT) Q2 CAPEX combined $155B · 3× the $52.5B same quarter 2024. Amazon $34.2B · Meta $43.4B · Google $34.0B · Microsoft $43.4B. AI-infra CAPEX cycle at historic scale.",
    bodyEn: "■ Data Details\n\nToday from Evan D on hyperscaler CAPEX:\n\n**Q2 2026 CAPEX By Company**\n- **Amazon (AMZN)**: $34.2B\n- **Meta (META)**: $43.4B\n- **Google (GOOGL)**: $34.0B\n- **Microsoft (MSFT)**: $43.4B\n- **Combined**: $155B\n\n**Year Comparison**\n- 2024 same quarter combined: $52.5B\n- Growth: 3× (about +195%)\n\n**Price (Reference)**\n- Alphabet Inc: $256.13\n\n■ Why This Data Matters\n\n1. **AI infra CAPEX historic high**: $155B/quarter = $620B/year pace. 3× vs 2024 · AI infra cycle at historic scale\n\n2. **META·MSFT $43.4B each**: Meta and Microsoft top per-company CAPEX · Reality Labs (META) / Azure (MSFT) infrastructure expansion\n\n3. **AMZN·GOOGL $34B**: Amazon and Google similar scale · AWS/GCP infrastructure sustained expansion\n\n4. **NVDA revenue growth signaled**: Substantial portion of hyperscaler CAPEX buys NVDA GPUs · NVDA revenue sustained growth signal\n\n■ Combined With Recent Flow\n\nRecent hyperscaler reports:\n- **7/24**: GOOGL 2026 CAPEX raised to $200B (from prior $60B)\n- **7/28**: OpenAI Ohio $500B DC (Softbank $250B backstop)\n- **7/29**: META×BLK 1 GW DC JV $14B\n- **7/30**: MSFT Q4 CAPEX +60% enterprise · AMZN Q2 imminent\n- **7/31**: MSFT Azure $100B · AMZN net income 3× · CAPEX $220B raise\n- **Today**: MSFT +$400B · AMZN detail · CAPEX combined $155B · cloud $142B\n\nMulti-layer indicators confirm hyperscaler CAPEX cycle expansion.\n\n■ CAPEX vs Revenue vs FCF Triangle\n\n**CAPEX**: $155B Q2 · record\n**Revenue**: Cloud infra Q2 $142B\n**FCF**: GOOGL Q2 first-negative -$5.9B (7/24) · MSFT/AMZN maintain positive\n\n**Implications**\n- CAPEX scale exceeds revenue scale = FCF pressure sustained\n- But revenue +43% YoY sustained = recovery cycle in progress\n- Hyperscalers focused on future revenue growth · sacrificing short-term FCF\n\n■ Each Company CAPEX Characteristics\n\n**META $43.4B**\n- Reality Labs hardware\n- AI infrastructure (today's separate BLK JV etc.)\n- Ad infrastructure\n\n**MSFT $43.4B**\n- Azure infrastructure\n- OpenAI partnership infrastructure\n- Copilot deployment\n\n**AMZN $34.2B**\n- AWS infrastructure\n- AI workload support\n- Retail/logistics (some)\n\n**GOOGL $34.0B**\n- GCP infrastructure\n- Anthropic collaboration (today's separate $15B DC etc.)\n- Search/YouTube AI integration\n\n■ Counter-view\n\n(1) Sustained CAPEX rise could pressure FCF · shareholder-return reduction risk, (2) Today's unusual_whales MSFT AI cyber attack + Aschenbrenner Fund liquidation etc. are AI cycle concern signals, (3) Recovery cycle normalization timing opaque · payback scenario risk, (4) Market reaction may differ on 2027 CAPEX further raise.\n\n■ Watch Next\n\n(1) 2027 CAPEX guidance (AMZN/MSFT etc.), (2) FCF vs CAPEX balance, (3) NVDA revenue segment detail (hyperscaler vs frontier AI), (4) Cloud revenue growth continuity.\n\ninvestus.kr SRP Chief Investment Officer",
