    bodyEn: "■ TOSV Summary Points\n\nItems from the Tesla Owners Silicon Valley bull frame today:\n\n- Record revenue $28.235B (+24% YoY beat), deliveries 480k+, energy storage record 21.6 GWh, services +50%\n- Cybertruck started at Fremont last week; Cybercab next\n- Robotaxi expanded to 40+ EU cities\n- Bay Area service expanded ~50%\n- S12 & S3 lite roll out FSD v14 to more HW3/HW4 vehicles\n- Training compute in Texas more than doubled in H1, coming online in Q3/Q4\n- Optimus Gen 3 production up +20% vs Gen 2\n\n■ Why the Summary Matters\n\nOverlaps with Cole Grinde's 15+ list but TOSV emphasizes quantitative datapoints from the recent print — Texas training compute doubling in H1 and Optimus Gen 3 +20%. It's essentially the shareholder-update content reframed from an owner-community perspective.\n\n■ Validation Axis\n\nWatch whether Texas training compute actually comes online in Q3/Q4 to accelerate FSD V15 training, and whether Optimus Gen 3 +20% is a sustainable growth pace.\n\ninvestus.kr SRP Chief Investment Officer",
