    bodyEn: "■ Context\n\nOn the Tesla Q2 earnings call, Elon Musk expressed strong optimism about the remaining months of 2026. Per Tesla Owners Silicon Valley's citation, Musk framed this as potentially one of Tesla's best years ever.\n\n■ Why This Framing\n\nOther information from the same call backs it up: Cybertruck starting at Fremont with Cybercab next, Robotaxi expanded to 40+ EU cities, Texas training compute doubled in H1 (Q3/Q4 online), Optimus Gen 3 production +20% vs Gen 2. If these multi-axis advances translate into earnings across the remaining 5 months, this CEO tone has substance.\n\n■ Temperature Gap With the Market\n\nAnalysts hearing the same print cut PTs en masse today, and TSLA dropped ~12%. The CEO bull tone and analyst downgrade tone clash head-on. The next quarter's print will determine which view gets validated.\n\ninvestus.kr SRP Chief Investment Officer",
