    summary:       "Tesla가 수요일 장 마감 후 Q2 2026 어닝 발표. 분기 인도는 480,126대(record, +25% YoY), Energy 21GWh. Robinhood 리테일 질문 7개(14.5M TSLA shares) 중 4개가 Robotaxi/Cybercab 관련. 최다 upvote 질문은 3분기 연속 후퇴한 Robotaxi 가이던스(US 50% 커버리지 → 7 metros). 지난 48시간 진전: Tampa/Orlando 오픈, Bay Area SF/Q, Cybercab Starlink V3, FSD v14 Lite HW3 롤아웃.",
    body:          "■ 원문 (Muskonomy / Tesla · 2026.07.21)\n\n\"NEWS: All eyes on Tesla's Q2 earnings call and retail investors on Robinhood.\n\nTesla reports Wednesday after market close.\n\n7 retail questions made the cut, carrying roughly 14.5M TSLA shares between them.\n\n4 of the 7 are about Robotaxi or Cybercab.\n\nThe most upvoted question is also the hardest.\n\n699 votes asking why Tesla has robbed short retail investors robotaxi guidance 3 earnings reports running, from 50% US coverage by the end of 2025 down to 7 metros in the past.\n\nThe 2 questions carrying the most shares are robotaxi expansion constraints at 5.4M and the Optimus Gen 3 ramp at 5.3M.\n\nShareholders want the factory deployment status and the 2027 external sales timeline.\n\nOne question asks Musk to commit to hitting at least half the 2025 compensation goals before entertaining any offer to acquire or merge Tesla. It carries 838,000 shares.\n\nTesla walks in with the operational numbers already public. 480,126 deliveries, a record and up 25% year on year, Energy storage at 21GWh with fresh batteries at Optimus factory ready to keep close to open question.\n\nThe last 48 hours handed Tesla fresh answers to most of what is being asked. Robotaxi opened in Tampa and Orlando, the Bay Area service got SF/Q access, Starlink V3 was confirmed inside Cybercab and the wide FSD V14 Lite rollout to HW3 began.\n\n5 of the 7 cities Tesla named for the first half of 2026 are now live. Phoenix and Vegas are what is left.\n\n(Source: Tesla, July 21, 2026)\"\n\n■ 투자시사점\n\n어닝 콜의 관심은 실적보다 Robotaxi 가이던스와 Optimus Gen 3 ramp. 팩토리 배포 현황·2027 external sales 타임라인 코멘트가 리레이팅 트리거. 지난 48시간 이벤트가 이미 답 일부를 제공했으므로 실적 콜에서는 그 이상의 새 신호가 필요.\n\ninvestus.kr SRP 최고투자책임자 발행",
    titleEn:       "TSLA — Q2 2026 Earnings Preview (Wed AMC · Record Deliveries 480,126)",
    summaryEn:     "Tesla reports Q2 2026 after market close on Wednesday. Q2 deliveries are a record 480,126 (+25% YoY) with 21 GWh in energy storage. 7 retail questions from Robinhood carry ~14.5M TSLA shares — 4 of 7 focus on Robotaxi/Cybercab. Top-upvoted question challenges Tesla on robotaxi guidance receding across 3 earnings (US 50% coverage → 7 metros). Past 48h: Tampa/Orlando launched, Bay Area SF/Q access, Cybercab Starlink V3, wide FSD v14 Lite rollout to HW3.",
    bodyEn:        "■ Source (Muskonomy / Tesla · 2026.07.21)\n\n\"NEWS: All eyes on Tesla's Q2 earnings call and retail investors on Robinhood.\n\nTesla reports Wednesday after market close.\n\n7 retail questions made the cut, carrying roughly 14.5M TSLA shares between them.\n\n4 of the 7 are about Robotaxi or Cybercab.\n\nThe most upvoted question is also the hardest.\n\n699 votes asking why Tesla has robbed short retail investors robotaxi guidance 3 earnings reports running, from 50% US coverage by the end of 2025 down to 7 metros in the past.\n\nThe 2 questions carrying the most shares are robotaxi expansion constraints at 5.4M and the Optimus Gen 3 ramp at 5.3M.\n\nShareholders want the factory deployment status and the 2027 external sales timeline.\n\nOne question asks Musk to commit to hitting at least half the 2025 compensation goals before entertaining any offer to acquire or merge Tesla. It carries 838,000 shares.\n\nTesla walks in with the operational numbers already public. 480,126 deliveries, a record and up 25% year on year, Energy storage at 21GWh with fresh batteries at Optimus factory ready to keep close to open question.\n\nThe last 48 hours handed Tesla fresh answers to most of what is being asked. Robotaxi opened in Tampa and Orlando, the Bay Area service got SF/Q access, Starlink V3 was confirmed inside Cybercab and the wide FSD V14 Lite rollout to HW3 began.\n\n5 of the 7 cities Tesla named for the first half of 2026 are now live. Phoenix and Vegas are what is left.\n\n(Source: Tesla, July 21, 2026)\"\n\n■ Investment Implications\n\nCall attention shifts from numbers to Robotaxi guidance and Optimus Gen 3 ramp. Commentary on factory deployment and 2027 external sales timeline = re-rating triggers. The past-48h events already answered part of the retail questions, so the call needs additional new signals to move the stock.\n\ninvestus.kr SRP Chief Investment Officer",
