    title:         "FSD v14 Lite — 400만 구형 HW3 차량에 wide release 예정",
    summary:       "Tesla VP AI Ashok Elluswamy가 X에서 확인: v14 lite는 destination 주차 옵션을 표시하고 Blue P를 대체하는 소형 빌드로, AI distillation을 통해 HW4 V14 소프트웨어의 주행 방식을 HW3에 학습시킨다. 약 400만 구형 HW3 차량에 wide release 예정이며, 2025 초 이후 HW3의 첫 major FSD 업그레이드다. 주차·후진·merge·traffic lights·pedestrian 처리가 개선되며 여전히 supervised 시스템으로 유지된다.",
    body:          "■ 원문 (Muskonomy, Ashok Elluswamy on X · 2026.07.20)\n\n\"Tesla's FSD v14 Lite is likely heading to a wide release for about 4 million older cars.\"\n\nAshok Elluswamy, Tesla's VP of AI, revealed that a smaller build called v14 lite is being used to show you your parking options at destination. It removes the Blue P and you can press it to start FSD in park.\n\nThe upgrade uses AI distillation to teach the older HW3 computer how the newer HW4 V14 software drives, the first major FSD jump for those cars since early 2025.\n\nOwners get new parking, unparking and reversing, plus smoother handling of merges, forks, traffic lights and pedestrians. It stays a supervised system, but it is the biggest step forward HW3 has seen in a year.\n\n■ 투자시사점\n\n구형 400만 차량의 소프트웨어 재활성화 = 구독 매출 회수 + 데이터 파이프라인 재확장. v14 Lite의 destination 주차 UI가 Blue P를 대체하는 형태로 상용 로보택시 조작 방식과 근접해가는 신호.\n\ninvestus.kr SRP 최고투자책임자 발행",
    titleEn:       "FSD v14 Lite — Wide Release Coming to ~4M Older HW3 Cars",
    summaryEn:     "Tesla VP AI Ashok Elluswamy revealed on X that v14 lite is a smaller build that shows destination parking options and replaces Blue P. The upgrade uses AI distillation to teach older HW3 how the newer HW4 V14 software drives — the first major FSD jump for those cars since early 2025. Owners get new parking, unparking, reversing, plus smoother merges, traffic lights, pedestrians. Still supervised, but the biggest step HW3 has seen in a year.",
    bodyEn:        "■ Source (Muskonomy · Ashok Elluswamy on X · 2026.07.20)\n\n\"Tesla's FSD v14 Lite is likely heading to a wide release for about 4 million older cars.\"\n\nAshok Elluswamy, Tesla's VP of AI, revealed that a smaller build called v14 lite is being used to show you your parking options at destination. It removes the Blue P and you can press it to start FSD in park.\n\nThe upgrade uses AI distillation to teach the older HW3 computer how the newer HW4 V14 software drives, the first major FSD jump for those cars since early 2025.\n\nOwners get new parking, unparking and reversing, plus smoother handling of merges, forks, traffic lights and pedestrians. It stays a supervised system, but it is the biggest step forward HW3 has seen in a year.\n\n■ Investment Implications\n\nReactivating the software layer on ~4M older cars = subscription recapture + broader data pipeline. The Blue P → destination parking UI shift aligns with commercial robotaxi interaction patterns.\n\ninvestus.kr SRP Chief Investment Officer",
