    title:         "Giga Berlin — 배터리 셀 18 GWh 확장 · 총 투자 $1.4B · +40,000대/년 · +5,000 일자리",
    summary:       "Giga Berlin FY2025 Management Report(2026.06.25 제출): 2026 회계연도 생산량 유의미 증가 예상, 현재 30개국 공급. 배터리 셀 제조 capacity를 최대 8 GWh에서 18 GWh로 재상향, 셀 제조 총 투자액 약 $1.4B USD. Q3 2026부터 주간 7,000대(+30%)로 생산 확장하며 신규 일자리 5,000개·연간 40,000대 추가. Q3 2026 vehicle sales + energy 사상 최고 예상.",
    body:          "■ 원문 (Sawyer Merritt · Giga Berlin FY2025 Management Report, filed 2026.06.25)\n\n\"Tesla in a new Giga Berlin report just filed in recent weeks:\n\n'For the 2026 financial year, the company forecasts a significant increase in production volume compared with the previous year and assumes a corresponding increase in capacity utilization. Currently, more than 30 markets are supplied from Giga Berlin. It is planned to open up further markets in the future.\n\nThe decision was made to make further investments in the production capacity of battery cell manufacturing in order to realize a capacity of up to 8 GWh per year (this has since been raised to 18 GWh). For this purpose, the company will further invest in the necessary infrastructure. The total investment volume for cell manufacturing amounts to nearly $1.4 billion USD, according to Giga Berlin's Management Report for Fiscal Year 2025 filed on June 25, 2026.\n\nA lot of this was known, as Tesla recently announced that its plans to add roughly another 30% to Giga Berlin factory by another 20% to 7,000 vehicles per week starting in October of 2026 or Q3 2026. This shift in the production output was previously announced a few months ago. All this will result in 5,000 additional jobs at the plant, 40,000 vehicles per year.\n\nTesla had its best-ever Q3 in 2026 for both vehicle sales and energy deployments. We'll be interesting to see what happens in Q3 and Q4.'\"\n\n■ 투자시사점\n\n원가 축(셀 제조 in-house 확대) + 캐파 확장(7000대/주) + 매출 축(30개국+ 확대) 삼각. 5,000 신규 일자리는 유럽 정치·규제 우호도에도 긍정. Q3/Q4 실적 가이던스가 검증 축.\n\ninvestus.kr SRP 최고투자책임자 발행",
    titleEn:       "Giga Berlin — Battery Cell Capacity Raised to 18 GWh · ~$1.4B Invest · +40k Cars/yr · +5k Jobs",
    summaryEn:     "Giga Berlin FY2025 Management Report (filed 2026.06.25): significant 2026 production volume increase expected, 30+ markets supplied. Battery cell capacity raised from up to 8 GWh/yr to 18 GWh, total cell invest ~$1.4B USD. Output +30% to 7,000 cars/week from Q3 2026, +5,000 jobs, +40,000 cars/yr. Q3 2026 vehicle sales + energy expected to set new records.",
    bodyEn:        "■ Source (Sawyer Merritt · Giga Berlin FY2025 Management Report, filed 2026.06.25)\n\n\"Tesla in a new Giga Berlin report just filed in recent weeks:\n\n'For the 2026 financial year, the company forecasts a significant increase in production volume compared with the previous year and assumes a corresponding increase in capacity utilization. Currently, more than 30 markets are supplied from Giga Berlin. It is planned to open up further markets in the future.\n\nThe decision was made to make further investments in the production capacity of battery cell manufacturing in order to realize a capacity of up to 8 GWh per year (this has since been raised to 18 GWh). For this purpose, the company will further invest in the necessary infrastructure. The total investment volume for cell manufacturing amounts to nearly $1.4 billion USD, according to Giga Berlin's Management Report for Fiscal Year 2025 filed on June 25, 2026.\n\nA lot of this was known, as Tesla recently announced its plans to add roughly another 30% to Giga Berlin factory by another 20% to 7,000 vehicles per week starting in October of 2026 or Q3 2026. This shift in the production output was previously announced a few months ago. All this will result in 5,000 additional jobs at the plant, 40,000 vehicles per year.\n\nTesla had its best-ever Q3 in 2026 for both vehicle sales and energy deployments. We'll be interesting to see what happens in Q3 and Q4.'\"\n\n■ Investment Implications\n\nCost axis (in-house cell) + capacity axis (7k/wk) + revenue axis (30+ markets) triangle. 5,000 new jobs also strengthens EU political/regulatory tailwind. Q3/Q4 guidance = verification axis.\n\ninvestus.kr SRP Chief Investment Officer",
