    bodyEn:        "■ Source (Muskonomy · 2026.07.20)\n\n\"Tesla builds the stripped-down Model Y Standard at Giga Berlin and prices it near 40,000 euros, about 10,000 below the Premium version, after European sales slid last year.\n\nNew numbers show why this bold matters. A study by the International Council on Clean Transportation and Fraunhofer ISI found comparable electric cars in Germany got about 18% cheaper since 2020, adjusted for inflation, while combustion cars rose about 27%.\n\nBut the median electric car still jumped 42% to about 53,000 euros, because most brands pushed buyers toward bigger, pricier models. That left the affordable end thin, right where Tesla's Standard Model Y sits.\n\n(Source: ICCT and Fraunhofer ISI via Reuters, July 18)\"\n\n■ Investment Implications\n\nTesla fills the affordable-EV void others left open. \"Go low when everyone else pushes premium.\" Verify via European sales recovery & monthly registrations.\n\ninvestus.kr SRP Chief Investment Officer",
