    bodyEn:        "■ Source (Eva McMillan · 2026.07.20)\n\n\"Ron Baron thinks $SpaceX will claim $10,000 per share in 10 years thanks to Elon Musk's Optimus.\"\n\n■ Fact-Check Note\n\n• Optimus is Tesla's (TSLA) humanoid robot program\n• Ron Baron has consistently used Optimus as an anchor for the Tesla long-term upside narrative\n• The original tweet's ticker ($SpaceX) contradicts the underlying argument (Optimus) — most naturally read as a ticker typo by Eva McMillan\n• Publishing verbatim would misfile this under SPCX — separated as TSLA report instead\n\n■ Investment Implications\n\nBaron's upside frame is a long-term narrative, not a confirmed catalyst. Optimus commercialization timing, production ramp, and unit economics are the verification axes. Useful as a long-term anchor separate from near-term events (earnings, FSD approvals).\n\ninvestus.kr SRP Chief Investment Officer",
